Fix: dnd-crawler calcAC() recursed infinitely, crashing combat.

The romance patch aliases calcAC then redeclares it with a *function declaration*.
Both declarations hoist, so the later one wins before any line executes and
_origCalcAC ends up pointing at the wrapper -- which then calls itself.

Proven by executing the real file headlessly (soloforte-testkit/rungame.mjs):
  before:  _origCalcAC === calcAC -> true,   calcAC() -> RangeError
  after:   _origCalcAC === calcAC -> false,  calcAC() -> 12  (base 10 + DEX 14 mod)

Apply:   git apply fix-dnd-calcac.patch
Verify:  node --stack-size=2000 ../soloforte-testkit/rungame.mjs

diff --git a/dnd-crawler.html b/dnd-crawler.html
index 8e5b680..2efc7d0 100644
--- a/dnd-crawler.html
+++ b/dnd-crawler.html
@@ -7573,20 +7573,20 @@ function getChatLines(comp) {
 
 // ============================================================
 // AC BONUS FOR ROMANCE
 // ============================================================
 // Patch calcAC to include beloved's shield
 const _origCalcAC = calcAC;
-function calcAC() {
+calcAC = function () {
   let ac = _origCalcAC();
   if (player && player.belovedShield && player.romanced) {
     const belovedInParty = (player.squad || []).some(c => c.name === player.romanced && c.hp > 0);
     if (belovedInParty) ac += 1;
   }
   return ac;
-}
+};
 
